mapping "V8219.1" source="V8219" target="214188005" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Swedish source = SNOMED CT 214188005 = streetcar occupant injured in collision with motor vehicle
        in traffic accident (base ICD-10 V82.1, Athena concept 45570994). The 5th-char suffix is a
        Swedish national extension encoding activity context (sport/leisure/work/etc.) with no
        OMOP/SNOMED CT representation; clinical accident content is identical to base V82.1. Primary SNOMED CT
        target 442458 = (Athena). Mapping rationale: the Swedish 5th-character activity suffix
        (idrott/lek/arbete/etc.) is a national-extension dimension with no SNOMED CT or OMOP analogue; the
        clinical accident content is fully captured by the base V82.X SNOMED CT target(s), so each SNOMED CT
        target subsumes the clinical meaning of the source (broader). Confidence (high): one-level
        breadth mismatch with a verified Athena crosswalk on the base ICD-10 V82.X parent.
        """
}
